{number: 105}
{title: Who Is On the Lord’s Side?}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Who is on the Lord's side? Who will serve the King?
[F] Who will be His [C] helpers, other [G7] lives to bring?
[C] Who will leave the world's side? Who will face the foe?
[F] Who is on the [C] Lord's side? Who for [G7] Him will [C] go?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C] By Thy call of mercy, by Thy grace divine,
We are [F] on the [C] Lord's side—Savior, [G7] we are [C] Thine!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Not for weight of glory, nor for crown and palm,
[F] Enter we the [C] army, raise the [G7] warrior psalm;
[C] But for Love that claimeth lives for whom He died:
[F] He whom Jesus [C] loveth halts on [G7] neither [C] side.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Jesus, Thou hast bought us, not with gold or gem,
[F] But with Thine own [C] lifeblood, for Thy [G7] diadem;
[C] With Thy blessing filling each who comes to Thee,
[F] Thou hast made us [C] willing, Thou hast [G7] made us [C] free.
{end_of_verse}
